Stencicrity for Debian
======================

Which releases this package installs on
---------------------------------------

Stencicrity needs Shapely 2, so the .deb installs on releases that ship
python3-shapely 2.0 or newer:

  * Debian 13 (trixie) and newer - python3-shapely 2.1.0, python3 3.13
  * Ubuntu 24.04 LTS (noble) and newer - python3-shapely 2.0.3, python3 3.12

It does not install on Debian 12 (bookworm, python3-shapely 1.8.5) or on
Ubuntu 22.04 LTS (jammy, python3-shapely 1.8.0). Neither bookworm-backports
nor noble-backports carries a newer Shapely, so on those releases use a
virtualenv (pip install stencicrity) instead of the package.

The package itself is architecture: all and contains only Python code, so the
same file works on every architecture of a supported release.

Building
--------

The source is native (debian/source/format is "3.0 (native)"): the Debian
packaging lives in the upstream git tree and there is no separate upstream
tarball. Build it from a checkout with

  dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b

The release workflow in .github/workflows/release.yml does exactly that inside
a debian:trixie container, after setting the changelog version from the git
tag with dch.

